[- Reference: Includes. -]
[page id='includes'
  [meta
    title='Includes'
    layout='reference'
    nav-order='450'
    audience='user'
    summary='Two include forms, one resolver — parse-time for static composition, eval-time for dynamic.'
  ]

  [section id='two-forms' title='Two Forms, One Resolver'
    [prose CX has two include directives that share one resolver. The parse-time form expands files before the document reaches downstream tools; the eval-time form expands files while a CXL template runs. Both are opt-in via --include-root and both enforce the same containment rules.]
  ]

  [section id='parse-time' title='Parse-Time Include'
    [prose The parse-time form is the directive [?cx include=path]. The path resolves against --include-root; the directive is replaced in-place by the included document. Use this for static composition — config files, schema fragments, page templates whose paths are known up-front.]
    [code lang='shell' src='cx --cx --include-root=./conf main.cx']
    [code lang='cx' src='''[users
  [?cx include=lib/admins.cx]
  [user name=carol]]''']
  ]

  [section id='eval-time' title='Eval-Time Include'
    [prose The eval-time form is the directive [?include path]. The path is any CXL expression — literal, bound variable, or computed via filters. The included file parses with includes resolved inside it, and evaluates inline at the directive site.]
    [code lang='cx' src='[?include 'layouts/page.cxl']']
    [code lang='cx' src='[?include [?concat ['layouts/', meta/@layout, '.cxl']]]']
  ]

  [section id='security' title='Security and Cycle Detection'
    [prose Both forms reject absolute paths (E901), paths that escape the root after lexical normalisation (E902), and URL-shaped paths (E903). Cycle detection (E904) and depth limits (E905, default 8) protect against runaway recursion. See spec/include.md for the full error catalog.]
  ]

  [section id='related' title='Related'
    [list
      [item path='reference/cxl'  label='CXL language reference']
      [item path='reference/cli'  label='--include-root flag']
    ]
  ]

  [preserve id='author-notes'
    [- Hand-written notes survive regeneration. Empty by default. -]
  ]
]
